# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?

# Xcode — build artifacts
build/
DerivedData/
*.xcarchive
*.app
*.dmg

# Xcode — user-specific
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcscmblueprint
*.moved-aside

# Xcode — SHARED schemes are TRACKED, deliberately.
# Every scheme used to live in the gitignored xcuserdata/ above, autocreated by
# whoever happened to open the project. A clean clone therefore had nothing to
# build BY NAME, which is why gmVibes could never be built in CI and why
# build-dmg.sh's `-scheme GMVibes` only worked on a machine that had already
# opened Xcode. The negation is explicit so a future tidy-up of the
# user-specific block above cannot take the shared schemes with it.
!**/xcshareddata/
!**/xcshareddata/**

# Build output. gmk/.build/DerivedData is where every SCRIPTED xcodebuild lands
# (gm_build.sh's gm_xcb); ⌘R keeps Xcode's default DerivedData. The unanchored
# entries also cover any stray SwiftPM output, e.g. from the vendored package.
.build/
.swiftpm/
gmk/.build/

# xcode-build-server's parsed-flags cache, written beside buildServer.json at
# the repo root. buildServer.json itself is COMMITTED; the cache is per machine.
/.compile

# Distribution / signing secrets
ExportOptions.plist
*.p12
*.cer
*.provisionprofile
notarytool-*.json

# plugins/gmcc/bin/ is COMMITTED: gm_mcp and gm_hook ship inside the plugin
# (build_plugin_binaries.sh), and a marketplace install has no other way to get them.

# The gmbeta ALIAS tree — a second emit of the bridge under the name `gmbeta`,
# generated by generate_plugin.sh beside `gmcc`. It exists ONLY as a
# `claude --plugin-dir` target for beta/test GMVibes panes (so the working tree
# loads without colliding with the marketplace `gmcc`), has NO entry in
# marketplace.json, and is regenerated on every Beta build (PluginBridge) or
# manual generate. So it is a build artifact, not source: ignored, never
# committed.
plugins/gmbeta/

# The plugin DIRECTORY is not ignored and did not move: .claude-plugin/
# marketplace.json still registers `./plugins/gmcc`, and its commands/, skills/,
# hooks/ and .mcp.json are all still there. Only the Swift package left it.
